                                        <div class="thread">
              <div class="parent-box">
                  <article class="post post-parent">
          <div class="body"><p>For the second time this week Trump glitches and makes a weird sound mid speech.</p><p>I have zero knowledge of what would cause this strange speech behavior, and if anyone knows, I am all ears.</p><p>This is not AI. This is from 4:23 in this video:<br><a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/o_PJ61ycYfM?si=8d-yTRcKDTYIkrAa" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="invisible">https://www.</span><span class="ellipsis">youtube.com/live/o_PJ61ycYfM?s</span><span class="invisible">i=8d-yTRcKDTYIkrAa</span></a></p><p><a class="mention hashtag" href="https://mastodon.social/tags/trumpglitch" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#<span>trumpglitch</span></a></p></div>
            <footer>
      <span>@randahl@mastodon.social</span>      <a href="https://mastodon.social/@randahl/117492783895843968" rel="noopener"><time datetime="2026-10-23T23:20:05.000Z">4d ago</time></a>
    </footer>
  </article>
              </div>
              <div class="reply-arrow">&#8627; replied</div>
                <article class="post">
          <div class="body"><p><span class="h-card"><a class="mention" href="https://mastodon.social/@randahl" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@<span>randahl</span></a></span> when I was a kid my Furby would do this when it's batteries got too low. Has anyone checked the US Presidonts batteries?</p></div>
            <footer>
            <a href="https://mastodon.nervesocket.com/@ThaMunsta/117493121456957590" rel="noopener"><time datetime="2026-10-24T00:45:56.607Z">4d ago</time></a>
